?</b> Every input has exactly one arrow leaving it. Yes.","nodes":{"a0":{"cls":"good"},"a1":{"cls":"good"},"a2":{"cls":"good"},"a3":{"cls":"good"}},"edges":{"a0-b0":"muted","a1-b1":"muted","a2-b2":"muted","a3-b3":"muted","b0-a0":"hide","b1-a1":"hide","b2-a2":"hide","b3-a3":"hide"},"stats":[["Function?","yes"],["Injective?","?"],["Surjective?","?"]]},{"caption":"<b>Injective?</b> No two arrows land on the same output. Yes: from any output you can trace back to a single input.","nodes":{"b0":{"cls":"good"},"b1":{"cls":"good"},"b2":{"cls":"good"},"b3":{"cls":"good"}},"edges":{"a0-b0":"muted","a1-b1":"muted","a2-b2":"muted","a3-b3":"muted","b0-a0":"hide","b1-a1":"hide","b2-a2":"hide","b3-a3":"hide"},"stats":[["Function?","yes"],["Injective?","yes"],["Surjective?","?"]]},{"caption":"<b>Surjective?</b> Every output is hit by at least one arrow. Yes.","nodes":{"b0":{"cls":"good"},"b1":{"cls":"good"},"b2":{"cls":"good"},"b3":{"cls":"good"}},"edges":{"a0-b0":"muted","a1-b1":"muted","a2-b2":"muted","a3-b3":"muted","b0-a0":"hide","b1-a1":"hide","b2-a2":"hide","b3-a3":"hide"},"stats":[["Function?","yes"],["Injective?","yes"],["Surjective?","yes"]]},{"caption":"Verdict: a <b>bijection</b>: a perfect pairing.","nodes":{},"edges":{"a0-b0":"muted","a1-b1":"muted","a2-b2":"muted","a3-b3":"muted","b0-a0":"hide","b1-a1":"hide","b2-a2":"hide","b3-a3":"hide"},"stats":[["Function?","yes"],["Injective?","yes"],["Surjective?","yes"]]},{"caption":"Because it is a bijection, reversing every arrow still gives exactly one arrow per element: that reversed machine is the <b>inverse function</b> f<sup>−1</sup>.","nodes":{},"edges":{"a0-b0":"hide","a1-b1":"hide","a2-b2":"hide","a3-b3":"hide","b0-a0":"a","b1-a1":"a","b2-a2":"a","b3-a3":"a"},"stats":[["Function?","yes"],["Injective?","yes"],["Surjective?","yes"]]}]}]}